Nolderan sprints across the turf toward an orc locked in combat with Daren. In full stride, the ex-sage launches into a horizontal leap, twisting mid-air to slam both boots square into the monster's spine. The orc stumbles forward off-balance as Nolderan hits the grass on his shoulder. Daren drives his broadsword down through the warrior's collar before the brute can turn. Nolderan rolls clear of a counter-swing from a second orc, springs to his feet, and fakes a wide overhead slash with his left blade. As the orc jerks his shield up to intercept, Nolderan's right sword whips around in a low arc, shearing clean through the warrior's neck.

The haze of dwarven ale is still buzzing in the back of my skull, but standing idle isn't an option.

I draw my dagger and sprint toward the flank where Leila is fighting.

The nearest orc spots my approach, locking his shield forward to catch my thrust while driving a heavy spiked mace straight at my skull. With my blade committed, I can't parry the blow, leaving me no choice but to throw myself backward.

}
