ID: B2-Ch10a-Mammoth
TEXT:

We dive clear of the perimeter just as the blue light detonates upward, shooting thirty feet into the canopy. The clearing trembles beneath our boots. As the blinding glare burns away, a colossal shape takes form in the smoking grass.

A red-eyed mammoth towers over the clearing, easily thirty feet tall, its crimson eyes sweeping over us. Normal mammoths are only slightly larger than common elephants, but northern red-eyed mammoths are mountain terrors. Their hides are thick, natural armor plates far harder than elven steel, their trunks hit like iron battering rams, and their curved tusks can skewer a horse whole. A wild one might pause before attacking, but a summoned beast obeys only the master who called it.

The beast lets out a deafening trumpet that shakes the pines. In the distance, the faint pressure of the retreating orcs snaps shut as their mages teleport them away.

"Captain and casters are gone," Arraka announces from the amulet. "Just so you know."

"We can feel the empty air, Arraka," Illuna says through Flower. "They only stayed long enough to finish the summoning ritual. We need to clear the wyverns before more riders drop in."

Flower leaps into the air, twin columns of fire launching her skyward. Kate conjures an ice slab beneath her boots, encasing herself in an open ice cage as the platform rises.

"Keep that beast occupied while we clear the sky," Kate calls down. "Don't get yourselves killed."

"Easier said than done," Daren mutters, raising his shield.

"Leave the monster to us," Nolderan says, twin blades ready. "Daren and I haven't met a beast we couldn't bring down. Go handle the flyers."

Kate nods once, guiding her ice platform higher as she and Flower close the distance to the wyverns. Below, the mammoth stands motionless in the churned mud, small red eyes tracking our every shift in weight.

"So..." Hadrik mutters, rolling his shoulders. "Do we hit it, or what?"

choice("Suggest that we back off, slowly, while facing the mammoth", B2-Ch10a-Suggest, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10a-Suggest)
choice("Shoot the mammoth with the crossbow", B2-Ch10a-Shoot, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10a-Shoot)


ID: B2-Ch10a-Suggest
TEXT:

"It's testing our reaction," I say in a low voice. "In the wild, standard procedure with a northern mammoth is to yield ground slowly without breaking eye contact. If the summoning compulsion leaves it any instincts, it might let us back away. Step back slowly."

"You're the bookworm," Hadrik grunts. "Everyone ease back."

We retreat three paces into the brush, boots sliding through the damp needles. The mammoth watches us with unblinking red eyes. Then its ears flare, and it charges, thirty tons of muscle and bone tearing up the earth.

"So much for diplomacy!" Hadrik roars. "Brace yourselves!"

The dwarf sprints directly at the charging beast, launching himself twenty feet into the air with a hammer fist cocked for the forehead. The mammoth doesn't flinch. It plants its forelegs, swings its massive trunk like a club, and swats Hadrik out of the sky.

Hadrik crashes into the dirt with an impact that leaves a crater two feet deep.

"One clean blow from that trunk will snap every bone in your body," Daren says, staring at the crater. "Stay out of reach unless you're certain of your footing. Barry, your weapons won't bite through that plate hide. Leila, your blades have sharper enchantments. Help us draw its legs."

"I'm with you," Leila writes in quick blue letters.

"Move fast," Daren says, drawing his broadsword. "Hadrik can't take that punishment forever."

As Daren, Nolderan, and Leila spread out to flank the beast, a passage from my notebook flashes through my mind. I spent half a day studying northern beasts before the arena bouts. Standard weapons can't pierce the hide, but every creature has an anatomical blind spot.

I turn on my heel and sprint toward the camp. Melindra's tent flap is still zipped shut. There's no chance she slept through the horn blast and the ground-shaking roar. She's staying inside so no one sees her struggle with her wind magic.

I don't have time to worry about her pride right now.

I duck through my tent flap, unbuckle my pack, and yank out the leather-bound notebook. I flip through the creature diagrams until I reach the entry on northern mammoths. The anatomy sketch has three lines pointing to specific vulnerabilities.

choice("Continue", B2-Ch10a-Weakness, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10a-Weakness)


ID: B2-Ch10a-Shoot
TEXT:

"No time like the present," I say, raising my weapon.

I center the sights on the mammoth's forehead and loose a bolt. The steel tip strikes the thick bone plate with a dull thud and ricochets into the trees without leaving a scratch. The mammoth's red eyes lock onto me instantly. Its ears flare, and it charges, thirty tons of muscle and bone tearing up the earth.

"Hold on, big fellow!" Hadrik roars. "Take a swing at me!"

The dwarf sprints directly at the charging beast, launching himself twenty feet into the air with a hammer fist cocked for the forehead. The mammoth doesn't flinch. It plants its forelegs, swings its massive trunk like a club, and swats Hadrik out of the sky.

Hadrik crashes into the dirt with an impact that leaves a crater two feet deep.

"One clean blow from that trunk will snap every bone in your body," Daren says, staring at the crater. "Stay out of reach unless you're certain of your footing. Barry, your weapons won't bite through that plate hide. Leila, your blades have sharper enchantments. Help us draw its legs."

"I'm with you," Leila writes in quick blue letters.

"Move fast," Daren says, drawing his broadsword. "Hadrik can't take that punishment forever."

As Daren, Nolderan, and Leila spread out to flank the beast, a passage from my notebook flashes through my mind. I spent half a day studying northern beasts before the arena bouts. Standard weapons can't pierce the hide, but every creature has an anatomical blind spot.

I turn on my heel and sprint toward the camp. Melindra's tent flap is still zipped shut. There's no chance she slept through the horn blast and the ground-shaking roar. She's staying inside so no one sees her struggle with her wind magic.

I don't have time to worry about her pride right now.

I duck through my tent flap, unbuckle my pack, and yank out the leather-bound notebook. I flip through the creature diagrams until I reach the entry on northern mammoths. The anatomy sketch has three lines pointing to specific vulnerabilities.

choice("Continue", B2-Ch10a-Weakness, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10a-Weakness)


ID: B2-Ch10a-Weakness
TEXT:

The main vulnerability sits on the underside of the trunk, right at the base where it meets the jaw. Unlike standard elephants, red-eyed mammoths draw air through twin breathing slits tucked under the root of the trunk. There's no armored plate there, only soft mucous membrane. A deep blade thrust into that pocket will collapse the creature's airway. The catch is reaching the base of the trunk without getting flattened by thirty feet of thrashing muscle.

The eyes are an option, but the heavy brow ridge and thick, leathery lids make piercing them from the front nearly impossible once the beast closes its guard.

I shove the notebook into my pocket and run back out into the clearing. The mammoth is swinging its trunk in wide arcs, keeping Hadrik airborne while Daren, Nolderan, and Leila hack fruitlessly at the armored hide around its ankles. Hadrik leaps from a fresh crater, throws a punch, and crashes into the turf a third time.

Nobody on the ground can reach the airway at the base of the skull. Hadrik is busy being a target, and Kate and Flower are locked in dogfights with the wyvern riders.

We need another caster who can lift someone into the air.

"Melindra!" I shout, turning toward her closed tent. "Can you hear me?"

Nothing moves behind the green canvas.

"You don't have to show your face," I call out, pitching my voice over the thudding impacts of the fight. "Remember how you carried us over the outer wall at Thilias? I need you to lift me, but with reactive currents that follow my body movement. Leaning forward to accelerate, arms to steer. I've used wind magic twice before, and the theoretical foundation is sound. You've spent six centuries with air spells. You must know how to cast a kinetic current!"

choice("Continue", B2-Ch10a-Currents, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10a-Currents)


ID: B2-Ch10a-Currents
TEXT:

I wait, listening over the roar of the mammoth, but the green fabric doesn't shift.

"Listen," I call out. "I'm not asking you to step into the fight. You don't have to show yourself. Just give me the lift."

Silence.

"Come on, Melindra. I know you're awake."

Three seconds tick by.

"Melindra!"

A sudden coil of cold air tightens around my ribs, lifting me off the turf before I can brace. My boots leave the grass, rising three, five, eight feet into the air. When I shift my weight forward, the draft surges behind my shoulders, carrying me ahead. Raising my hands lifts my altitude; lowering them arrests my momentum. The kinetic currents latch onto the angle of my hips and knees, turning my leg movements into rudder control.

#if(v_b2_ch10_toast == 1 && v_b2_ch9_drink == 1) {
It lacks the instant response of the stat device's emergency flight mode, but for an external spell, the handling is remarkably fluid. Every tight bank sends a surge of ale-induced vertigo through my inner ear, but I can manage the balance.

"Much obliged!" I shout toward the tent, banking into a steep climb toward the canopy to run a quick handling check.

I practice hard turns, dives, and sudden stops. One miscalculated drift near that mammoth, and its trunk will pulp me against the dirt. My flight line has to be clean.

"Barry, above you!" Kate's warning cuts through the wind.

Two black wyverns peel out of the clouds in a steep dive, lances leveled straight at my chest. Kate and Flower are locked in midair combat with four other riders, too far to intercept.

}
#if(v_b2_ch10_toast == 0 || v_b2_ch9_drink == 0) {
It lacks the instant response of the stat device's emergency flight mode, but for an external spell, the handling is remarkably fluid.

"Much obliged!" I shout toward the tent, banking into a steep climb toward the canopy to run a quick handling check.

I practice hard turns, dives, and sudden stops. One miscalculated drift near that mammoth, and its trunk will pulp me against the dirt. My flight line has to be clean.

"Barry, above you!" Kate's warning cuts through the wind.

Two black wyverns peel out of the clouds in a steep dive, lances leveled straight at my chest. Kate and Flower are locked in midair combat with four other riders, too far to intercept.

}
choice("Try to attack the wyverns", B2-Ch10a-Wyverns, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10a-Wyverns, v_b2_ch10_bribe = 0)
choice("Aim to kill the orc riders first", B2-Ch10a-Riders, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10a-Riders, v_b2_ch10_bribe = 1)
choice("Try to bribe the orcs into joining my side", B2-Ch10a-Bribe, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10a-Bribe, v_b2_ch10_bribe = 2)


ID: B2-Ch10a-Bribe
TEXT:

"Hold!" I yell, waving an open hand as they plunge toward me. "You speak Common! We don't have to spill blood. Let's talk business!"

"We make no deals with human vermin!" the lead orc snarls. "We answer only to Tyrath!"

He thrusts his lance forward. I kick my legs, slipping beneath the steel point by inches, and come about in a tight turn.

"Only Tyrath?" I call out. "What if I match what the dragon pays and double it?"

"Our honor belongs to the dragon king!" the first rider barks.

"Wait a moment," the second rider cuts in, pulling his beast up alongside his partner. "How much gold are we talking about?"

#if(v_b2_ch6_crossbow == 1 && v_ch10_gems == 0 && v_ch3_treasure == 0 && v_b2_ch5_scimitar != 2) {
I pull my belt pouch loose and untie the cord, showing the handful of gold coins resting at the bottom. The lead orc lets out a harsh, barking laugh.

"You expect us to betray the lord of monsters for pocket change?"

"It's all the coin on me," I say. "Turn your beasts around, and it's yours."

"Enough talk," the lead rider sneers. "Brother, skewer him."

Both wyverns bank around, diving back toward me with lances lowered.

}
#if(v_b2_ch5_scimitar == 2 && v_ch10_gems == 0 || v_b2_ch6_crossbow == 0 && v_ch10_gems == 0 || v_ch10_gems == 0 && v_ch3_treasure != 0) {
I pull my belt pouch loose and untie the cord, showing the handful of gold coins resting at the bottom. The lead orc lets out a harsh, barking laugh.

"You expect us to betray the lord of monsters for pocket change?"

"I have more in my pack on the ground," I say quickly. "Give me a minute to fetch it."

"Enough talk," the lead rider sneers. "Brother, skewer him."

Both wyverns bank around, diving back toward me with lances lowered.

}
#if(v_ch10_gems == 1) {
I reach into my belt pouch and feel the hard, faceted edges of the gems inside. Loose coins won't tempt seasoned raiders, but a cut jewel is an entire fortune.

I pull out a polished ruby the size of a walnut and hold it high in the morning light. The red facets catch the sun, casting deep crimson glints across the orcs' faces.

"I have more in my pack," I say. "I'll give you this ruby upfront. Help me clear the remaining riders, and you get a flawless diamond to go with it. What do you say?"

The second orc stares at the jewel, his grip on his lance loosening. "A pretty stone, human. But where does an orc spend imperial gems? Tyrath's domain is the only territory that takes us. Human cities would hang us from the gates."

"Fyron's camp," I say. "You know the name?"

"The goblin general?" The orc's brow knits in thought. "Word in the barracks says his settlement took in half the western tribes last winter. Monies and monsters of every stripe."

"Are you out of your mind?" the first orc yells, glaring at his companion. "This is treason against the dragon!"

"Treason?" the second orc spits back. "Tyrath pays us in gristle and broken iron. Why bleed for a tyrant who treats us like fodder? This stone buys an estate in Fyron's lands. Think, brother!"

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch10a-Wyverns, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10a-Wyverns) if (v_ch10_gems == 0)
choice("Continue", B2-Ch10a-Bribe2, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10a-Bribe2) if (v_ch10_gems == 1)


ID: B2-Ch10a-Bribe2
TEXT:

set(v_ac_b2_ch10_creative,1)
achievement("A creative solution",v_ac_b2_ch10_creative)
"You are no brother of mine," the loyalist snarls, wrenching his wyvern's reins to drive his spear straight at the other orc's throat.

The mercenary rider is faster. He pulls up on his mount, rising above the thrust, and plunges his lance down through the loyalist's collarbone. The dead warrior slips from his saddle, tumbling through the empty air into the pines below.

"The deal is struck, human!" the surviving orc roars, brandishing his crimson lance.

"Here's your advance," I say, tossing the ruby across the gap.

The orc snatches the gem from the air with thick claws, tucking it into his belt sash. "Point me at the targets."

"Traitor!" another rider screams from above, diving his mount toward us with leveled steel.

My new ally doesn't flinch. He banks hard into a climb and rams his lance deep into the attacking wyvern's chest. The beast folds its wings with a dying shriek, plummeting toward the clearing with its rider pinned beneath it.

"What is happening down there?" Kate calls out from her ice platform, freezing two wyverns in mid-glide.

"The rider in gray is on our side!" I shout back. "Hold your fire on him!"

"Fine!" Kate and Illuna call back in unison, already redirecting their assault toward the remaining flyers.

"I'm heading down to crack the mammoth," I tell the mercenary orc. "Keep the sky clear."

I dip my shoulder, letting the wind currents plunge me down toward the ground battle.

choice("Continue", B2-Ch10a-Trample, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10a-Trample)


ID: B2-Ch10a-Riders
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_combat_technique < 3)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_combat_technique >= 3)

I drop into a steep dive to build momentum, then throw my weight upward, pedaling my legs against the wind currents to check my descent and bring my body vertical. My years flying aircraft kick in naturally, turning wind shear and banking angles into second nature.

Controlling direction with my lower body leaves both hands free for the crossbow. I level the weapon at the lead rider, tracking his trajectory as he closes the distance.

#if(v_combat_technique < 3) {
Leading an airborne target while floating on unstable air currents proves too erratic. My shots go wide, glancing off saddle leather or whistling into the empty sky. The magazine clicks empty. Before I can draw a sidearm, the second rider maneuvers into my blind spot. His lance drives into my gut, the iron point tearing through muscle and bone. As my vision greys out, he jerks the shaft free and drives it through my throat.

}
#if(v_combat_technique >= 3) {
I read the rider's flight arc and lead his helmet by half a yard. The bolt punches straight through the side of his skull, pitching him out of his leather harness. His mount screeches in confusion, banking erratically. I pump three bolts into the second rider's path, forcing him into a predictable climb, then dive directly from above to drive my dagger into the base of his neck.

Both riders tumble to the ground. I reload my magazine on the descent, steering down toward the mammoth.

}
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_combat_technique < 3)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_combat_technique < 3)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_combat_technique < 3)
choice("Continue", B2-Ch10a-Trample, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10a-Trample) if (v_combat_technique >= 3)


ID: B2-Ch10a-Wyverns
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_strength == 0)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_strength >= 1)

I drop into a steep dive to build momentum, then throw my weight upward, pedaling my legs against the wind currents to check my descent and bring my body vertical. My years flying aircraft kick in naturally, turning wind shear and banking angles into second nature.

Controlling direction with my lower body leaves both hands free for the crossbow. I aim directly for the lead wyvern's chest and empty the magazine in rapid succession. The steel bolts tear through its breastbone. The beast shrieks, crumpling its wings mid-dive, and crashes into the clearing with its rider crushed underneath.

The second wyvern closes before I can reload. Its leathery jaws snap open inches from my face. I draw my dagger with my right hand and drive the blade into its throat.

#if(v_strength == 0) {
The thick neck muscles resist the cut. My thrust lacks the power to reach the artery, and the blade jams in the gristle. Before I can wrench it free, the beast's jaws clamp down on my shoulder, shattering the bone, while the rider's lance punches through my chest.

}
#if(v_strength >= 1) {
The reinforced steel sinks to the hilt. Dark blood sprays across my arm as the wyvern thrashes in agony, spiraling out of control. The rider loses his stirrup grip, tumbling past my feet into the forest canopy below.

As the dying beast plummets after him, I slot fresh bolts into my crossbow and descend toward the ground battle.

}
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_strength == 0)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_strength == 0)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_strength == 0)
choice("Continue", B2-Ch10a-Trample, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10a-Trample) if (v_strength >= 1)


ID: B2-Ch10a-Trample
TEXT:

#if(v_b2_ch10_bribe == 2 && v_ch10_gems == 1) {
While I was tied up with the flyers, the mammoth has shifted targets, attempting to trample Daren and Nolderan into the dirt. The two swordsmen have been hacking at the beast's lower joints, bleeding its hocks and forcing it into clumsy, staggering charges. Unable to corner Daren, Nolderan, or Leila, the beast has turned its fury back on Hadrik, who continues to hammer away at its flank.

I drop into a steep dive to close the distance, then kick upward, checking my descent with a treading motion to hover twenty paces above the beast's head.

My flight maneuvers leave my upper body completely steady. Which vulnerable point do I strike: the armored eye socket, or the unshielded nostrils beneath the base of the trunk?

}
#if(v_ch10_gems == 0 || v_b2_ch10_bribe != 2) {
While I was tied up with the flyers, the mammoth has shifted targets, attempting to trample Daren and Nolderan into the dirt. The two swordsmen have been hacking at the beast's lower joints, bleeding its hocks and forcing it into clumsy, staggering charges. Unable to corner Daren, Nolderan, or Leila, the beast has turned its fury back on Hadrik, who continues to hammer away at its flank.

I check my descent, stabilizing twenty paces above the beast's head.

Which vulnerable point do I strike: the armored eye socket, or the unshielded nostrils beneath the base of the trunk?

}
choice("Attack the eyes", B2-Ch10a-Plan, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10a-Plan, v_b2_ch10_weakpoint = 0)
choice("Attack the nostrils", B2-Ch10a-Plan, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10a-Plan, v_b2_ch10_weakpoint = 1)


ID: B2-Ch10a-Plan
TEXT:

#if(v_b2_ch10_weakpoint == 0) {
The eyes offer the clearest line of sight. Thick eyelids or not, steel bolts delivered at close range ought to punch through.

I drop lower into the draft. Hadrik is clinging to the mammoth's trunk with both arms as the beast thrashes, trying to whip him off against the pines.

"Barry!" Hadrik roars, his voice rising and falling with every violent swing. "You're flying!"

"Working on it!" I call back.

"Good! Team up on this thing! I'll anchor the trunk, you put a blade through its eye!"

"How are you going to pin a thirty-ton mammoth?"

}
#if(v_b2_ch10_weakpoint == 1) {
The breathing slits beneath the trunk base are the only completely unarmored tissue on the creature. A clean thrust there will collapse the airway and end the fight.

I drop lower into the draft. Hadrik is clinging to the mammoth's trunk with both arms as the beast thrashes, trying to whip him off against the pines.

"Barry!" Hadrik roars, his voice rising and falling with every violent swing. "You're flying!"

"Working on it!" I call back.

"Good! Team up on this thing! I'll anchor the trunk, you hit the weak point!"

"I'm aiming under the jaw," I shout back. "How are you going to pin the trunk?"

}
"Leave that to me!" Hadrik releases his grip, dropping twenty feet into the mud. "Keep it occupied for five seconds while I take a new form!"

Shapeshifting against a red-eyed mammoth? If he transforms into a full-sized giant, Golmyck will disqualify him on the spot for breaking tournament size restrictions.

I don't have time to second-guess him. The mammoth spots me hovering above its tusks and lashes out with its trunk, the heavy tip whistling past my ears. I bank left, climbing out of its reach, then dive back in to hold its attention.

When the beast slows its flailing, I glance down.

Hadrik has turned into a giant mottled snail. He is oozing across the trampled grass at a pace that wouldn't catch a dead turtle. I pray he has an actual plan beyond providing comedy for the monster.

#if(v_b2_ch10_toast == 0 || v_b2_ch9_drink == 0) {
I slip past two more furious swings before Hadrik shifts back into his dwarf shape. He stands knee-deep in the thick white puddle his snail form left behind, arms outstretched, waving me down.

}
choice("Continue", B2-Ch10a-Breed, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10a-Breed) if (v_b2_ch10_toast == 0 || v_b2_ch9_drink == 0)
choice("Continue", B2-Ch10a-Drunk, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10a-Drunk) if (v_b2_ch10_toast == 1 && v_b2_ch9_drink == 1)


ID: B2-Ch10a-Drunk
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_reflexes < 4)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_reflexes == 4)
#if(v_reflexes < 4) {
I bank through three more tight turns, but the dwarven ale finally catches up with me. The world spins sideways. Nausea slams into my gut, throwing off my sense of up and down. By the time my vision clears, the mammoth's trunk is already half a foot from my chest.

The impact hits with the force of an avalanche. My ribs shatter inward, and the light dies.

}
#if(v_reflexes == 4) {
I bank through three more tight turns, but the dwarven ale finally catches up with me. The world spins sideways. Nausea slams into my gut, throwing off my sense of up and down.

With pure instinct, I kick hard against the air current, throwing my torso backward. The trunk whistles past my face, missing my nose by two inches. The gust of displaced wind nearly strips the clothes off my shoulders. I blink the haze from my eyes and focus.

Below, Hadrik shifts back into his dwarf shape. He stands knee-deep in the thick white puddle his snail form left behind, arms outstretched, waving me down.

}
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_reflexes < 4)
choice("Load from last checkpoint", , v_chapter_save_counter = 5, special:checkpoint_load) if (v_reflexes < 4)
choice("Load game", , , special:saves) if (v_reflexes < 4)
choice("Continue", B2-Ch10a-Breed, v_current_scene = B2-Ch10a-Breed) if (v_reflexes == 4)


ID: B2-Ch10a-Breed
TEXT:

set(v_is_dead,1) if (v_b2_ch10_weakpoint == 0 && v_strength < 4 || v_b2_ch10_weakpoint == 1 && v_b2_ch5_scimitar == 0 && v_reflexes < 2)
set(v_is_dead,0) if (v_b2_ch10_weakpoint == 0 && v_strength == 4 || v_b2_ch10_weakpoint == 1 && v_reflexes >= 2 || v_b2_ch10_weakpoint == 1 && v_b2_ch5_scimitar != 0)
#if(v_b2_ch10_weakpoint == 0 || v_b2_ch5_scimitar == 0) {
"Bait the swing over here!" Hadrik bellows, planting his feet wider.

The plan clicks into place. Northern giant snails secrete a thick mucus that cures on contact with air into an unbreakable adhesive. With his boots welded to the clearing's bedrock, Hadrik has the leverage to anchor the mammoth's trunk without being thrown.

"Hold steady!" I yell, banking into a steep descent.

I hover four feet in front of Hadrik, waving both arms. The mammoth takes the bait instantly, bringing thirty tons of momentum behind an overhead trunk strike. I kick backward on the draft a fraction of a second before impact. Hadrik lunges, wrapping both arms around the thick trunk and clamping down with all his giant-born strength.

"Go!" Hadrik grunts, teeth gritted as the beast strains violently. "The glue won't hold forever!"

The earth groans and fractures beneath the dwarf's boots as the mammoth tries to wrench itself free. I surge upward on a gust of wind.

}
#if(v_b2_ch10_weakpoint == 1 && v_b2_ch5_scimitar != 0) {
"Bait the swing over here!" Hadrik bellows, planting his feet wider.

The plan clicks into place. Northern giant snails secrete a thick mucus that cures on contact with air into an unbreakable adhesive. With his boots welded to the clearing's bedrock, Hadrik has the leverage to anchor the mammoth's trunk without being thrown.

"Hold steady!" I yell, banking into a steep descent.

I hover four feet in front of Hadrik, waving both arms. The mammoth takes the bait instantly, bringing thirty tons of momentum behind an overhead trunk strike. I kick backward on the draft a fraction of a second before impact. Hadrik lunges, wrapping both arms around the thick trunk and clamping down with all his giant-born strength.

"Go!" Hadrik grunts, teeth gritted as the beast strains violently. "The glue won't hold forever!"

The earth groans and fractures beneath the dwarf's boots as the mammoth tries to wrench itself free. I surge upward on a gust of wind.

I close the distance to the underside of the jaw in a heartbeat, spotting the twin breathing slits tucked behind the base of the trunk. I drive my scimitar straight into the opening, burying twenty inches of curved steel into the soft airway, and wrench the hilt in a full circle.

The mammoth's trumpet breaks into a wet, choking rattle. I yank the blade free and bank away as dark blood cascades across the turf. The beast staggers, wheezing frantically through ruined tissue, its legs giving out one by one until thirty tons of carcass crashes into the clearing with a bone-jarring thud.

}
#if(v_b2_ch10_weakpoint == 0 && v_b2_ch5_scimitar == 0 && v_strength < 4) {
I level my crossbow at the mammoth's eye from point-blank range and squeeze the trigger. The beast blinks instinctively. The heavy bolts ricochet off the thick brow and armored eyelid with dull metallic thuds. Cursing, I drop the crossbow, draw my dagger, and dive directly into the eye socket, driving the blade down with both hands.

My strike lacks the raw power to breach the dense cartilage. The steel jams halfway through the lid. Before I can wrench it free, the mammoth tears its trunk from Hadrik's grip and whips it across the sky, swatting me into paste against the clearing floor.

}
#if(v_b2_ch10_weakpoint == 0 && v_strength < 4 && v_b2_ch5_scimitar != 0) {
I level my crossbow at the mammoth's eye from point-blank range and squeeze the trigger. The beast blinks instinctively. The heavy bolts ricochet off the thick brow and armored eyelid with dull metallic thuds. Cursing, I drop the crossbow, draw my scimitar, and dive directly into the eye socket, driving the blade down with both hands.

My strike lacks the raw power to breach the dense cartilage. The steel jams halfway through the lid. Before I can wrench it free, the mammoth tears its trunk from Hadrik's grip and whips it across the sky, swatting me into paste against the clearing floor.

}
#if(v_b2_ch10_weakpoint == 0 && v_b2_ch5_scimitar == 0 && v_strength == 4) {
I level my crossbow at the mammoth's eye, but the bolts glance harmlessly off the armored lid as the beast blinks shut. I holster the weapon, draw my dagger, and drive my entire weight behind a point-first plunge into the eye socket.

Reinforced with four points of physical enhancement, the blade punches straight through the armored lid and sinks deep into the brain cavity. The mammoth convulses violently, shuddering from ears to tail, and collapses into the mud with a ground-shaking crash.

}
#if(v_b2_ch10_weakpoint == 0 && v_strength == 4 && v_b2_ch5_scimitar != 0) {
I level my crossbow at the mammoth's eye, but the bolts glance harmlessly off the armored lid as the beast blinks shut. I holster the weapon, draw my scimitar, and drive my entire weight behind a point-first plunge into the eye socket.

Reinforced with four points of physical enhancement, the steel punches straight through the armored lid and sinks deep into the brain cavity. The mammoth convulses violently, shuddering from ears to tail, and collapses into the mud with a ground-shaking crash.

}
#if(v_b2_ch10_weakpoint == 1 && v_b2_ch5_scimitar == 0 && v_reflexes < 2) {
I close on the underside of the jaw and drive my dagger into the unarmored breathing slit, twisting the blade through the soft tissue. The beast roars in pain, but the dagger's short blade fails to reach the primary windpipe.

The mammoth wrenches its trunk free from Hadrik's hold, curls the tip backward into an arc, and brings it down like a sledgehammer onto my spine. The blow crushes my ribs against the beast's jaw, ending my life before I hit the grass.

}
#if(v_b2_ch10_weakpoint == 1 && v_b2_ch5_scimitar == 0 && v_reflexes >= 2) {
I close on the underside of the jaw and drive my dagger into the unarmored breathing slit, twisting the blade through the soft tissue. The beast roars, tearing its trunk free from Hadrik's grip to whip the tip backward at my skull.

With enhanced reflexes, I yank the blade clear and kick hard against the air draft, rolling beneath the swinging trunk by a hair's breadth. The laceration inside the throat is fatal. The mammoth stumbles, clutching at its throat with its trunk as it chokes on its own blood, and crashes dead into the mud with a thunderous impact.

}
choice("Restart game", Ch1-Intro1, v_current_scene = Ch1-Intro1, special:restart) if (v_b2_ch10_weakpoint == 0 && v_strength < 4 || v_b2_ch10_weakpoint == 1 && v_b2_ch5_scimitar == 0 && v_reflexes < 2)
